  - created_at: "2026-10-16T07:34:04.040Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Latest full review remediation: preserve original create aliases in cycle validation after keyed upsert, including one or two matched rows; reject missing, non-array and empty MCP mutation arguments before planning; reject an explicit stdin channel beside a file before reading either. The real CLI exposed a shared SDK forwarding defect: normalized options had overwritten every Commander source with cli, misclassifying default-true stdin as explicit input. Synchronization now retains known parser origins, with an independent regression and default/explicit/file compatibility controls. Five final regression cases fail at the intended assertions on the isolated unchanged ae5b722 head; the corrected four-file suite passes 98 tests, four-project typecheck, focused ESLint and generated contracts. Corrected SDK prose and release report spacing through supported PM annotation edits. The generated tracker reflow preserves every unrelated metadata value and annotation provenance; whitespace-only text changes and verified immutable history retain the original dated observations. The release and runtime-admission owners remain open and unclaimed."
  - created_at: "2026-10-16T07:45:31.432Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Test-audit control: malformed and duplicate aliases already refuse on the unchanged head because excludeOwnCreateIds collects the original aliases before matching. Three adjacent hypothesis controls passed on that baseline. Retained the five demonstrated regressions and the existing validation order; removed the redundant prospective tests and unnecessary call reordering. The cycle defect is different: its graph previously omitted aliases after their rows became updates."
  - created_at: "2026-10-16T07:47:35.695Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Final local verification: all four linked commands pass 148 tests. The real CLI integration independently rejects explicit file plus stdin selection and still accepts the default file route; all 13 IO cases pass. All nine packaged npx/bunx workflows pass, the SDK surface has zero classified changes, and the unchanged first-party artifact budget passes at 19,101,201 bytes across 1,678 files with the complete 4,745-file runtime closure. Four TypeScript projects, generated contracts and focused ESLint pass. The five demonstrated pre-fix regressions remain recorded in the isolated control. Final hosted static, source coverage and full review are required after this commit; earlier qualified local admission failures remain historical evidence, without any budget or timeout waiver."
  - created_at: "2026-10-16T08:13:40.677Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Hosted b98f152 passes full source coverage and every required runtime, analyzer and consumer check; static stops at the exact CLI refusal census because the newly implemented explicit input-channel guard changes the observed count from five to six. Declared that additional site as transport validation before SDK dispatch, preserving the existing ownership and exact count matching. The real census gate now passes with zero violations and no applied waivers; all 18 linked classification controls pass, including fail-closed mismatch behavior. The prior 148 functional cases remain passed on the same runtime source. Final whole-head static and full review must pass before merge."
  - created_at: "2026-10-16T08:54:27.795Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "The latest full review leaves one private comparator-contract nit: equal strings should compare as zero. The non-less branch now converts string inequality to its numeric result, preserving minus one and plus one for unequal keys and yielding zero for equality. The existing selected linked suite passes 91 SDK, CLI and MCP cases, including public canonicalization and Unicode key-order controls. Generated contracts, focused lint and the unchanged SDK surface pass. The helper remains private and the current distinct-key callers retain their ordering. Final-head checks and another full review remain required."
  - created_at: "2026-10-16T09:55:57.409Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Final review clarification: SDK replay guidance now describes successful committed transactions with an unchanged resolved plan. Own-created IDs remain excluded from upsert matching; external matches, schema changes or document edits require a new ID only when they change that committed plan. Existing SDK/CLI replay controls still pass: 91 linked SDK/CLI/MCP cases. Final wording passes pnpm build and pnpm quality:docs-links. The future release reminder and GH-1484 intake remain separately owned and unclaimed."
  - created_at: "2026-10-16T09:58:58.190Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
