    text: "Post-changelog artifact measurement: the final runtime candidate passes the unchanged 20000000-byte first-party ceiling at 19111072 bytes / 1682 files, retaining 4745 runtime files. This measurement includes the newly generated raw-duration fix changelog entry; earlier package measurements remain dated observations."
  - created_at: "2026-10-16T13:43:06.162Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Latest full-review remediation: core camelCase option targets normalize to stored snake_case keys after declared-field resolution; the regression commits six core-field upserts with distinct transaction ids and retains one item. The linked SDK/CLI/MCP command passes 87 tests. Three exact filtered regressions fail on isolated unchanged 53aa49473, including the boolean-list public CLI case owned by the scalar-validation item. No public API shape, numeric budget or guard is weakened."
  - created_at: "2026-10-16T14:04:24.076Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Final local acceptance: 10540 tests pass with three skips and exact source coverage: 69207/69207 statements, 53134/53134 branches, 14251/14251 functions and 65701/65701 lines. The scalar/loader/CLI linked command passes 137 cases and the SDK/CLI/MCP command passes 87. Three filtered regressions fail on isolated unchanged 53aa49473. Nine packed npx/bunx workflows, four typecheck projects, focused lint, docs links and generated contract/error/capability/SDK surface checks pass. Final-head hosted checks and full review remain required."
  - created_at: "2026-10-16T14:35:38.101Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Verified the final normalization boundary with a real schema-capable extension: camelCase metadata legacyId is not a runtime-schema declaration and must retain its exact stored spelling. The new regression fails on unchanged d62719229 and the corrected five-file SDK/CLI/MCP command passes 88 tests. The core vocabulary is now shared privately between document validation and normalization, avoiding a public SDK export or duplicated field list. Known core option aliases still normalize; unrelated extension keys are preserved. Typecheck, lint, docs links, docstrings, error catalogue and unchanged SDK surface checks pass."
  - created_at: "2026-10-16T14:53:54.039Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Final source run result is qualified: 10539 tests passed, three skipped and two existing aborted-rebase-recovery cases timed out at their unchanged 30000ms limit. No coverage-summary artifact was generated, so this run is not a 100-percent coverage receipt. Retain the failed full-run record and rerun those cases in isolation without increasing a deadline. The linked SDK/CLI/MCP command passes 88 tests, including the actual extension camelCase regression; final exact-head hosted coverage remains required."
  - created_at: "2026-10-16T15:00:20.903Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Current candidate acceptance: 88 SDK/CLI/MCP linked cases pass, including real extension metadata legacyId preservation and six core alias upserts. The one new regression fails on unchanged d62719229. Four-project typecheck, focused lint, docs/skills links, docstrings, generated wrappers/contracts/error/capability/SDK checks and nine packed npx/bunx workflows pass. The complete local run is qualified: 10539 passed, three skipped, two existing 30-second Git-recovery timeouts; those two pass unchanged in isolation. No local final 100-percent coverage claim is made. Require the final hosted coverage check before merge."
  - created_at: "2026-10-16T15:23:35.213Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Full review at 8a7be4106 identified a wrapped document upsert alias gap: normalized core metadata lookup precedes item-document conversion and misses camelCase fields. Investigating both lookup and persistence behavior before changing the shared SDK boundary; 26 required checks on 8a7be4106 pass."
  - created_at: "2026-10-16T15:48:24.214Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Final wrapped-document review fix: shared metadata-key resolution now governs pre-upsert document lookup and document-to-options conversion. Known core camelCase names persist under their canonical keys, exact stored keys win when both spellings appear, and declared/unrelated extension metadata spelling remains preserved. Lookup-only remediation was insufficient because persistence must use the same identity. 89 linked SDK/CLI/MCP cases pass. The new wrapped-alias regression fails on unchanged 8a7be4106 with upsert_key_missing and passes after the fix; it proves create, matched update, persisted snake_case metadata, exact stored-key precedence and one retained item. The complete local run passes 10542 tests with three skips and exact 100/100/100/100 coverage: 69219 statements, 53148 branches, 14254 functions and 65708 lines, all covered. Four-project typecheck, ESLint, documentation links/docstrings, zero-change public SDK surface and nine packed npx/bunx consumers pass. Final-head hosted checks and renewed full review remain required before merge."
  - created_at: "2026-10-16T16:28:06.738Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: Full review on 65e05f248 found unique-key scan caching remains stale after intervening batch updates/closes/releases; also document both overload declarations and implementation to satisfy the unchanged static export-docstring gate.
  - created_at: "2026-10-16T17:09:10.536Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Unique-key cache review remediation: invalidate after successful update/close/release and include earlier creates in rescans. Keep lazy scans for uninterrupted create-only batches. Document every overload declaration and implementation without changing the static gate. 94 linked SDK/CLI/MCP tests and eight catalog-generator tests pass; nine packed npx/bunx consumers pass. Five uniqueness scenarios cover updates into and away from conflicts, updates to an earlier created item, close and release. Old 65e05f248 fails the controls; the close fixture now supplies a valid terminal-create reason and old code incorrectly accepts it. Source static assurance passes, including the original 100% export-docstring threshold. The wider local static command stopped on cleared expected fields for the two reopened owners; concrete expectations were restored through PM. Full local source execution records 10546 passes, three skips and one unchanged MRTR task-status wait failure; that case passes alone and no final local coverage artifact exists. Final-head hosted coverage and full review remain required. Hound stayed pending on 65e05f248 without a target URL; Chrome confirms this repository is active, but the dashboard has no job detail. New review-wait UX intake pm-jm7m3o is open and unclaimed."
  - created_at: "2026-10-16T18:03:48.593Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Create-cache review remediation: advance every cached key scan from the created item metadata rather than assuming the guard describes every field written. This handles unguarded and differently guarded records, actual normalized values and multiple matching ids without another project scan. Metadata absent on the created item is ignored consistently with candidate scans. The array control uses canonical lowercase guard values because tags normalize on write. 100 linked SDK/CLI/MCP tests and 10553 complete-source tests pass (three skipped). Exact source coverage is 100/100/100/100 with every one of 69226 statements, 53150 branches, 14253 functions and 65717 lines covered. Five current regressions fail on isolated unchanged 552ec58d0; the missing-metadata positive control passes there. Current cases prove unguarded creates, different guard keys/values, normalized tag arrays, omitted metadata and complete matching-id diagnostics. Typecheck, lint, the actual static source gate, zero-change SDK surface, contracts and nine packed npx/bunx consumers pass. A live candidate read at 18:00 UTC records one backend start/finish pair, zero failure and nine healthy stack services. Sentry still reports the two tracked unresolved faults, with empty recent trace/span discovery. Final-head hosted checks and renewed full review remain required."
  - created_at: "2026-10-16T19:08:38.387Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Final review corrections: source provenance is retained only when current and synchronized values are identical; changed parser/preflight overrides become explicit cli values. A supplied blank upsert key refuses before settings reads or writes instead of disabling keyed import. Only an omitted key selects plain creation; a resolved empty schema key reaches the established refusal rather than silently skipping upsert. Stored journal schema/version identity corruption now uses preservation-first transaction_journal_invalid, while valid step-plan differences retain transaction_plan_mismatch. 103 linked SDK/CLI/MCP tests and 39 registration-helper tests pass. Six current regression controls fail on isolated unchanged 2a13a6f23: changed default/environment origins, two blank-key SDK variants, CLI blank-key refusal and corrupt journal identity/schema classes. Corrupt journal bytes and pending step state are preserved. Existing valid-plan mismatch behavior remains covered. Typecheck, ESLint, actual source static quality, zero-change SDK surface, contracts, docs links and nine packed npx/bunx consumers pass. The latest full local run reached its unchanged 1200-second linked deadline and produced no final summary or coverage artifact; prior 2a13a6f23 source passed 10553 tests with exact global coverage. Final-head hosted coverage and renewed full review remain required."
  - created_at: "2026-10-16T19:35:19.107Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: Full review on 716fb6a5a found compensated create retries can adopt a closed item as applied. Preserve the closed item and refuse automatic retry until it is explicitly reopened or reconciled; use immutable compensation history rather than mutable close prose as ownership evidence. This avoids silently reviving later user edits or losing original lifecycle intent.
  - created_at: "2026-10-16T20:24:59.704Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Final create-retry review remediation: a closed target with immutable close-history evidence of this transaction compensation refuses with typed transaction_create_compensated (conflict4). Mutable close prose cannot bypass the guard. Explicitly reopening the retained item permits the same document to resume and replay with that creation open, without duplication. The current 105 SDK/CLI/MCP linked cases and 39 helper cases pass. Two retry variants and the format-neutral diagnostic regression fail on isolated prior716fb6a5a; three failures are at the intended assertions. Current complete-source execution is qualified by the unchanged1200-second deadline and missing final coverage artifact; require final-head hosted exact coverage. The additive error catalogue, public SDK snapshot, contracts and SDK retry documentation are updated; no budgets or deadlines were relaxed."
  - created_at: "2026-10-16T22:01:29.269Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Latest review refinement: inspect only the latest immutable close event when recognizing transaction compensation. A later explicit reopen followed by a user close is preserved on both first successful retry and committed replay. A terminal creation interrupted before journal recording also resumes without being mistaken for compensation. The 107-case linked SDK/CLI/MCP cohort passes; an isolated worktree at 81e35e54e59533410b359e407524cce750e24065 fails the new later-user-close regression while the terminal-create positive control passes. Four-project typecheck and focused ESLint pass. Final-head hosted exact coverage and renewed incremental review remain required; no coverage thresholds or review filters changed."
  - created_at: "2026-10-16T22:23:37.833Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Additional release review control: the public update --status closed path delegates to routeCloseStatusUpdate/runClose and already records the canonical close event. The c1dfe27 baseline passes all three focused controls (explicit close, routed status update and interrupted terminal creation), so the speculative broader history scan was discarded before commit. Production remains the reviewed latest-close predicate. The expanded108-case linked SDK/CLI/MCP cohort passes with that production implementation. Added the routed status update as a positive lifecycle preservation control and clarified the SDK documentation; typecheck and focused lint pass."
  - created_at: "2026-10-16T22:27:52.345Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Hosted c1dfe27 static gate identified a stale generated REFUSAL_CLOSURE_CENSUS: the new transaction_create_compensated catalogue entry was missing from its census. Regenerated through contracts:agent-surfaces:update; the census now lists419 codes and400 explicitly uncovered rows, retaining19 executable codes against the unchanged18-code ratchet. Generated agent surfaces, error catalogue and full command contract checks pass. This is a generated-document synchronization fix; the production latest-close predicate remains unchanged from c1dfe27. The final linked SDK/CLI/MCP cohort passes108 cases, including routed-update and interrupted-terminal positive controls."
  - created_at: "2026-10-17T02:29:03.210Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Post-merge delivery evidence: PR1479 reviewed head8b50e05799fa8bc587598308a763057de753bb39 merged as94757af3016420bfda6b6fc1905be7814ee2ea1d with the same tree. The final hosted source gate and tagged Release38991739473 each passed exact100/100/100/100 coverage with zero uncovered counts; the tagged cohort passed10567 tests. Final CodeRabbit delta reported no actionable comments and all threads were resolved; unavailable Sourcery/Greptile providers remain explicit limitations. Public2026.10.17 is latest, and fresh anonymous Node/Bun SDK plus CLI, npx and bunx checks passed. This completes the previously pending hosted/publication handoff without changing the immutable implementation-close evidence or treating the earlier local1200-second timeout as a successful full local run. Release and consumer evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/actions/runs/38991739473 ."
learnings[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-16T04:25:15.096Z","harness:codex",A workspace transaction lock serializes bulk transactions but does not fence ordinary item writers. Revalidate a planned match against the same document read under the target item lock; resolve shortened SDK ids to canonical identity before scoping a target-specific guard. Prove the race at the actual item-lock boundary with a separate ordinary writer and verify its history remains intact.
  "2026-10-16T07:31:18.265Z","harness:codex",Preserve Commander option origins when forwarding normalized SDK values. A default-true flag must remain a default; relabeling every value as CLI input breaks safe explicit-input conflict checks.
  "2026-10-16T18:03:49.466Z","harness:codex","A create guard covers only its own precondition; the record can write other keys or normalized values. Keep indexes current from returned item metadata across all cached keys, preserve all matching ids, and keep project scans lazy. Guard values must use the stored canonical representation, such as lowercase tags."
  "2026-10-16T19:08:39.545Z","harness:codex","Presence and provenance are semantic inputs: distinguish omitted options from explicitly blank values, preserve default origins only for unchanged values, and classify corrupt stored identity separately from a valid journal whose requested plan changed. Corruption recovery must preserve bytes and avoid advising a new id."
  "2026-10-16T20:06:54.828Z","harness:codex","A stable create id proves existence, not successful lifecycle state after rollback. Refuse a still-closed compensated creation using immutable close history, and require explicit reconciliation before adopting it on retry."
